.TH _EXIT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
_exit \- terminate without cleanup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B void _exit(int status);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Terminates the calling thread using the Linux exit syscall without invoking
Crunch finalizers. If it is the last thread, the process terminates and the
low eight bits of status are available to the parent.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Does not return.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR waitpid (3crunch),
.BR _exit (2)
